/* Práctica extra por unidad (escucha larga, habla libre y pronunciación). Se genera con tools/add-extra.js */
window.PRACTICE_EXTRA = [null,null,null,[[{"t":"listen","say":"I'd been working at the bank for almost ten years when they offered me the position in Madrid. At first I said no, because I'd just bought a flat, but by the end of the month I had changed my mind. By this time next year, I'll have been living here for five years.","q":"¿Por qué rechazó al principio el puesto en Madrid?","o":["Porque acababa de comprar un apartamento","Porque no hablaba español","Porque su jefe no quería","Porque el salario era bajo"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Sorry I'm late. I've been sitting in traffic for over an hour. Apparently, there had been an accident on the motorway, and by the time I got off at the next exit, half the city was doing the same thing.","q":"¿Qué causó el retraso?","o":["Un accidente en la autopista","Una huelga de transporte","Se quedó dormido","Una reunión larga"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"When I arrived at the station, the train had already left. I was furious, because I'd been running for ten minutes. Luckily, the next one was only twenty minutes later, so I wasn't late for the interview in the end.","q":"¿Llegó tarde a la entrevista?","o":["No, tomó el siguiente tren a tiempo","Sí, llegó una hora tarde","No fue a la entrevista","Sí, porque perdió dos trenes"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"This time next week, I'll be lying on a beach in Thailand. I'll have finished all my exams by then, so I won't have to think about university for a whole month.","q":"¿Qué estará haciendo la próxima semana?","o":["Estará en una playa en Tailandia","Estará presentando exámenes","Estará trabajando","Estará estudiando en la universidad"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"By the time she arrived, the film ___.","o":["had already started","has already started","already starts","was already starting yet"],"a":0,"x":"Una acción terminada antes de otra en el pasado va en past perfect."},{"t":"mc","q":"How long ___ English before you moved to London?","o":["had you been studying","have you been studying","are you studying","did you studied"],"a":0,"x":"Duración hasta un momento del pasado: past perfect continuous."},{"t":"fill","q":"By 2030, scientists ___ (find) a cure for many diseases.","ans":["will have found"],"x":"Future perfect: will have + participio."},{"t":"oral","text":"I'd been waiting for over an hour by the time she finally called."},{"t":"oral","text":"By the end of this year, I'll have been working here for a decade."},{"t":"talk","q":"Talk about a big change in your life. What had you been doing before, and how did things change?","min":35,"keys":[["had been"],["since","for"]],"model":"Before I moved to Bogotá, I had been living with my parents for twenty-five years. I had been working in a small shop, but since I moved, I have been working in an office and I feel more independent."},{"t":"talk","q":"Where will you be and what will you have achieved five years from now?","min":32,"keys":[["will have"],["will be"]],"model":"In five years I will be living in a bigger city and I will have finished my master's degree. I hope I will have travelled to Canada and I will be speaking English much more fluently."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the question and answer it with your own words.","min":20,"keys":[["have been"]],"model":"I have been learning English for about two years. I have been studying almost every day, mostly with this course and with series.","say":"How long have you been learning English, and what have you been doing to improve?"}],[{"t":"listen","say":"If I'd known how expensive the city centre was, I would have booked a hotel near the airport. Now I've spent half my budget on the first three nights, so I'll have to be very careful for the rest of the trip.","q":"¿Qué problema tiene el hablante?","o":["Gastó la mitad de su presupuesto en tres noches","Perdió su vuelo","El hotel estaba lejos del centro","Le robaron el dinero"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"I really wish I had studied medicine. My parents wanted me to, but I chose law because my friends were doing it. If I were younger, I'd go back to university, but with three kids and a mortgage, it's just not realistic.","q":"¿Por qué no vuelve a la universidad?","o":["Por sus hijos y la hipoteca","Porque no le gusta la medicina","Porque sus padres no quieren","Porque ya es médico"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Unless the weather improves, we'll have to cancel the outdoor concert. But if it stops raining by four, we can still set everything up in time. Either way, we'll let everyone know on social media by five.","q":"¿Qué pasará si deja de llover a las cuatro?","o":["Podrán montar todo a tiempo","Cancelarán el concierto","Cambiarán la fecha","Lo harán bajo techo"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Had I left the house five minutes earlier, I would never have met her. I missed my bus, sat on a bench to wait, and she sat down next to me. We've been married for twelve years now.","q":"¿Cómo conoció a su esposa?","o":["Esperando un bus después de perder el anterior","En el trabajo","En la universidad","Por internet"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"If you ___ me, I would have helped you.","o":["had told","told","have told","would tell"],"a":0,"x":"Tercer condicional: if + past perfect, would have + participio."},{"t":"mc","q":"I wish I ___ more time to travel. I'm always working.","o":["had","have","will have","would have had"],"a":0,"x":"Deseo sobre el presente: wish + pasado."},{"t":"fill","q":"If only I ___ (not say) that to her yesterday!","ans":["hadn't said","had not said"],"x":"Arrepentimiento sobre el pasado: if only + past perfect."},{"t":"oral","text":"If I had known about the meeting, I would have changed my plans."},{"t":"oral","text":"I wish I could speak English as fluently as my colleagues."},{"t":"talk","q":"Talk about a decision you regret. What would have happened if you had chosen differently?","min":27,"keys":[["if i had","if i'd"],["would have"]],"model":"If I had studied engineering, I would have had better job opportunities. I regret not taking that decision, but if I hadn't studied business, I wouldn't have met my wife."},{"t":"talk","q":"If you could change one thing about your city, what would it be and why?","min":26,"keys":[["if"],["would"]],"model":"If I could change one thing, I would improve public transport. If the buses were faster, people wouldn't use their cars so much and the air would be cleaner."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen and answer: what would you do?","min":26,"keys":[["would"]],"model":"If I won the lottery, I would buy a house for my parents, I would travel around the world and I would give some money to a children's hospital.","say":"Imagine you won the lottery tomorrow. What would you do with the money?"}],[{"t":"listen","say":"According to a report published yesterday, the number of people working from home has fallen by twelve percent since last year. However, the authors point out that most companies now allow at least one remote day a week.","q":"¿Qué dice el informe?","o":["Menos gente trabaja desde casa, pero la mayoría de empresas permite un día remoto","Todos volvieron a la oficina","El trabajo remoto aumentó un doce por ciento","Las empresas prohibieron el trabajo remoto"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The new bridge, which is said to be the longest in the country, was opened by the president this morning. It is expected to reduce journey times by up to forty minutes, although critics claim the project went three hundred million dollars over budget.","q":"¿Qué critican del puente?","o":["Costó mucho más de lo previsto","Es demasiado corto","Aumentará el tráfico","Se construyó sin permiso"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The minister told journalists that the government would not raise taxes this year. She added that the new hospital would be finished before the end of the summer, and that more teachers had already been hired.","q":"Según la ministra, ¿qué NO pasará este año?","o":["No subirán los impuestos","No terminarán el hospital","No contratarán profesores","No habrá elecciones"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"A man has been arrested after a valuable painting was stolen from the city museum on Sunday night. Police believe he may have had help from someone working inside the building. The painting has not yet been found.","q":"¿Qué creen los policías?","o":["Que alguien del museo pudo ayudarle","Que el cuadro ya fue recuperado","Que el ladrón actuó solo","Que el cuadro era falso"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"The suspect is believed ___ the country last week.","o":["to have left","leaving","that he left","to leave yet"],"a":0,"x":"Pasiva impersonal sobre el pasado: be believed to have + participio."},{"t":"mc","q":"She said she ___ the report the following day.","o":["would send","will send","sends","has sent"],"a":0,"x":"Estilo indirecto: will → would."},{"t":"fill","q":"The new law ___ (approve) by parliament last night.","ans":["was approved"],"x":"Pasiva en pasado simple: was + participio."},{"t":"oral","text":"It has been reported that the company will open three new offices next year."},{"t":"oral","text":"The suspect is thought to have escaped through a window at the back of the building."},{"t":"talk","q":"Tell a piece of news you heard recently. Use reported speech: what did people say?","min":35,"keys":[["said that","told"],["according to"]],"model":"Yesterday I read that the city will build a new metro line. According to the mayor, it will be ready in five years. She said that it would reduce traffic, but some experts told journalists that it was too expensive."},{"t":"talk","q":"Where do you usually get your news, and how do you know if it's reliable?","min":30,"keys":[["because"]],"model":"I usually get my news from websites and sometimes from the radio. I check if the information appears in more than one source, because there is a lot of fake news on social media."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the headline and explain it in your own words.","min":18,"keys":[["has been","was","were"]],"model":"The headline says that a new species of frog has been discovered in the Colombian rainforest by a team of scientists.","say":"Breaking news: a new species of frog has been discovered in the Colombian rainforest by an international team of scientists."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"Personally, I'm in favour of a four-day week. Not only does it improve people's well-being, but it also seems to increase productivity. That said, I can see it might be difficult for hospitals or shops that need to be open every day.","q":"¿Qué desventaja menciona?","o":["Puede ser difícil para hospitales y tiendas","Reduce la productividad","Empeora el bienestar","Es ilegal en muchos países"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"While I understand why some parents want to ban phones at school, I don't think it's the right solution. Instead, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly. After all, they'll need these skills for the rest of their lives.","q":"¿Qué propone el hablante?","o":["Enseñar a usar los teléfonos con responsabilidad","Prohibir los teléfonos en el colegio","Dar teléfonos a todos los estudiantes","Que los padres decidan"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Some people argue that tourism destroys local culture. However, in my experience, it can actually help preserve traditions, because tourists are willing to pay for traditional crafts, music and food. The key is how it's managed.","q":"¿Qué opina el hablante sobre el turismo?","o":["Puede ayudar a preservar tradiciones si se gestiona bien","Siempre destruye la cultura local","Debería prohibirse","Solo beneficia a los hoteles"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The main argument against nuclear energy is safety. Nevertheless, statistics show that it causes far fewer deaths per unit of energy than coal. The real problems, in my view, are the cost and what to do with the waste.","q":"Según el hablante, ¿cuáles son los verdaderos problemas?","o":["El costo y los residuos","La seguridad y las muertes","La falta de científicos","Que no produce suficiente energía"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"___ the high cost, the project was approved.","o":["Despite","Although","However","Even"],"a":0,"x":"Despite va seguido de un sustantivo."},{"t":"mc","q":"I agree to some extent. ___, I think there are other factors.","o":["However","Despite","Because of","Unless"],"a":0,"x":"However introduce una idea contraria al inicio de la frase."},{"t":"fill","q":"Not only ___ it cheaper, but it's also faster. (be)","ans":["is"],"x":"Inversión después de Not only: Not only is it..."},{"t":"oral","text":"On the one hand, technology makes life easier; on the other hand, it can be very addictive."},{"t":"oral","text":"Although many people disagree, I firmly believe that education should be free."},{"t":"talk","q":"Should university be free for everyone? Give your opinion with at least two arguments and one counter-argument.","min":29,"keys":[["in my opinion","i believe","i think"],["however","on the other hand","although"],["firstly","first of all","secondly","moreover"]],"model":"In my opinion, university should be free. Firstly, it gives everyone the same opportunities. Moreover, the country benefits from having more professionals. However, someone has to pay for it, so taxes might increase."},{"t":"talk","q":"Is it better to live in a big city or in a small town? Compare both.","min":28,"keys":[["whereas","while","on the other hand"],["better","more","less"]],"model":"Big cities offer more jobs and entertainment, whereas small towns are quieter and safer. On the other hand, life in a city is more expensive. Personally, I prefer a medium-sized city."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the opinion and say if you agree or disagree, and why.","min":27,"keys":[["agree","disagree"],["because"]],"model":"I partly agree. Social media can be useful to stay in contact with family, but I disagree that it makes us happier, because people often compare their lives with others.","say":"Social media has made us more connected and happier than ever before."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"I was absolutely exhausted after the trip. We'd been travelling for nearly twenty hours, and I could barely keep my eyes open. But the moment I saw the view from the hotel, I felt completely refreshed.","q":"¿Cómo se sintió al ver la vista?","o":["Completamente renovado","Aún más cansado","Decepcionado","Asustado"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"My boss keeps putting off the decision. Every time we bring it up, she says she needs more data. If she doesn't make up her mind soon, we'll run out of time to launch the product before Christmas.","q":"¿Cuál es el problema?","o":["La jefa sigue aplazando la decisión","La jefa ya canceló el producto","No hay suficientes empleados","El producto salió mal"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"It was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity, so I jumped at the chance. The salary wasn't great, but I learned more in that year than in the previous five. Looking back, it was the best decision I've ever made.","q":"¿Qué piensa ahora de esa decisión?","o":["Fue la mejor que ha tomado","Se arrepiente","Fue un error económico","No aprendió nada"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Honestly, the film was a bit of a letdown. The trailer looked fantastic, but the plot was predictable and the ending was rushed. The acting was decent, though, especially the main character.","q":"¿Qué le gustó de la película?","o":["La actuación, sobre todo del protagonista","El final","La trama","Nada"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"I'm not ___ hungry. I had a huge lunch.","o":["remotely","highly","deeply","strongly"],"a":0,"x":"Not remotely = para nada (colocación)."},{"t":"mc","q":"We need to ___ a decision before Friday.","o":["make","do","take up","give"],"a":0,"x":"La colocación es make a decision."},{"t":"fill","q":"I can't ___ up with this noise any longer! (put)","ans":["put"],"x":"Put up with = aguantar."},{"t":"oral","text":"It was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity, so I jumped at the chance."},{"t":"oral","text":"The film was a bit of a letdown, but the acting was absolutely brilliant."},{"t":"talk","q":"Describe the best or worst trip you have ever had. Use strong adjectives (amazing, exhausted, terrifying...).","min":30,"keys":[["absolutely","really","completely"],["amazing","terrible","exhausted","awful","fantastic","terrifying","stunning"]],"model":"The best trip I've ever had was to Cartagena. The old city was absolutely stunning and the food was amazing. On the last day we were completely exhausted, but it was totally worth it."},{"t":"talk","q":"Talk about a habit you'd like to give up or take up. Use at least two phrasal verbs.","min":26,"keys":[["give up","take up","cut down","put off","work out","carry on"]],"model":"I'd like to give up eating so much sugar and take up running. I keep putting it off, but I want to start working out three times a week."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen and describe the picture the speaker paints with your own words.","min":19,"keys":[["it seems","looks","there is","there are"]],"model":"It seems to be a small, peaceful village by a lake, with colourful wooden houses and mountains covered in snow behind it.","say":"Imagine a tiny village next to a crystal-clear lake, with colourful wooden houses and snow-covered mountains rising behind it."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"Good morning, everyone. Thanks for joining the call. The purpose of today's meeting is to review the third-quarter results and agree on next year's budget. Before we start, could everyone please mute their microphones when they're not speaking?","q":"¿Cuál es el propósito de la reunión?","o":["Revisar resultados y acordar el presupuesto","Presentar a un nuevo empleado","Hablar de las vacaciones","Despedir personal"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Thank you for calling. I'm afraid Mr Ortiz is in a meeting at the moment. Can I take a message? ... Certainly. So that's Laura Gómez from Delta Logistics, and you'd like him to call you back before three regarding the delayed shipment.","q":"¿Qué quiere Laura Gómez?","o":["Que el señor Ortiz la llame antes de las tres","Cancelar un pedido","Una reunión mañana","Hablar con recursos humanos"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"I'm calling to follow up on my application for the marketing coordinator position. I submitted it two weeks ago and I was wondering whether you had had a chance to review it. I'm very enthusiastic about the role and happy to provide any additional information.","q":"¿Por qué llama la persona?","o":["Para hacer seguimiento a su solicitud de empleo","Para quejarse del servicio","Para renunciar","Para pedir un aumento"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Let me just summarise what we've agreed. Marketing will send the new designs by Thursday, IT will update the website by the fifteenth, and we'll all meet again on the twentieth to check progress. Does that work for everyone?","q":"¿Qué hará el equipo de IT?","o":["Actualizar el sitio web antes del quince","Enviar los diseños el jueves","Organizar la reunión del veinte","Revisar el presupuesto"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"I look forward to ___ from you.","o":["hearing","hear","heard","be hearing"],"a":0,"x":"Look forward to + verbo con -ing."},{"t":"mc","q":"Could you ___ me know if the time suits you?","o":["let","make","say","tell to"],"a":0,"x":"Let me know = avísame."},{"t":"fill","q":"Please find ___ the documents you requested. (adjuntos)","ans":["attached"],"x":"Please find attached = adjunto encontrará."},{"t":"oral","text":"Thank you for your patience. I'll look into the issue and get back to you by the end of the day."},{"t":"oral","text":"Could we possibly move the meeting to Thursday afternoon instead?"},{"t":"talk","q":"Job interview: tell me about yourself. Present, past and future.","min":33,"keys":[["currently","i'm working","i work"],["before","previously"],["i'm looking for","i would like","i'd like"]],"model":"I'm currently working as a sales assistant in a technology company, where I deal with clients every day. Previously, I worked in a call centre for two years. Now I'm looking for a position with more responsibility."},{"t":"talk","q":"A customer calls angry because their order is late. Answer politely, apologise and offer a solution.","min":32,"keys":[["sorry","apologise","apologize"],["i'll","i will","we will","we'll"]],"model":"I'm really sorry about the delay. I completely understand your frustration. I'll check the status of your order right now, and if it doesn't arrive tomorrow, we will send you a new one free of charge."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to your manager's question and answer it professionally.","min":27,"keys":[["because","so"]],"model":"Yes, the project is on track. We've finished the design phase and we're now testing the app, so we should be ready to launch by the end of the month.","say":"Hi, can you give me a quick update on the project? Are we still on track for the launch?"}]],[[{"t":"listen","say":"What really frustrates me isn't the workload itself; it's the constant interruptions. It's not that I mind working late occasionally, but when every task gets interrupted by another 'urgent' request, nothing ever gets finished properly.","q":"¿Qué es lo que realmente le molesta?","o":["Las interrupciones constantes","La cantidad de trabajo","Trabajar tarde de vez en cuando","Su salario"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Never before had the company faced such a crisis. Not only were sales falling, but two of the directors resigned in the same week. It was only when the new CEO arrived that things began to stabilise.","q":"¿Cuándo empezó a mejorar la situación?","o":["Cuando llegó el nuevo director ejecutivo","Cuando renunciaron los directores","Cuando subieron las ventas","Nunca mejoró"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"It was my grandmother, not my parents, who taught me to cook. She never used recipes; she did everything by eye and by taste. What I remember most is the smell of her kitchen on Sunday mornings.","q":"¿Qué recuerda más el hablante?","o":["El olor de la cocina de su abuela los domingos","Las recetas escritas de su abuela","Las clases de cocina de sus padres","Un restaurante"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Little did I know, when I accepted that internship, that it would shape the rest of my career. I had only taken it because I needed the money, but by the end of the summer, I knew exactly what I wanted to do.","q":"¿Por qué aceptó la pasantía?","o":["Porque necesitaba el dinero","Porque sabía que quería esa carrera","Porque se la recomendó un profesor","Porque era obligatoria"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"Rarely ___ such a beautiful sunset.","o":["have I seen","I have seen","I saw","did I saw"],"a":0,"x":"Inversión tras adverbio negativo: Rarely have I seen..."},{"t":"mc","q":"___ I need right now is a long holiday.","o":["What","That","Which","It"],"a":0,"x":"Cleft sentence: What I need is..."},{"t":"fill","q":"It ___ my brother who broke the window, not me. (be, pasado)","ans":["was"],"x":"Cleft sentence con it: It was X who..."},{"t":"oral","text":"Not only did she win the competition, but she also broke the national record."},{"t":"oral","text":"What I find most impressive about her is her ability to stay calm under pressure."},{"t":"talk","q":"Talk about a person who has influenced you. Use at least one cleft sentence (What I admire... / It was... who...).","min":29,"keys":[["what i","it was","the thing"],["admire","taught","influenced","inspired"]],"model":"It was my first English teacher who really inspired me. What I admired most about her was her patience. What she taught me was not just grammar, but the confidence to make mistakes."},{"t":"talk","q":"Describe a moment that changed your life. Start with 'Never before...' or 'Little did I know...'.","min":30,"keys":[["never before","little did i","not until","only when"]],"model":"Little did I know that moving abroad would change my life completely. Never before had I felt so lonely, but only when I started speaking the language did I begin to feel at home."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen and react with emphasis: do you agree?","min":19,"keys":[["i do","what i","really"]],"model":"I do agree that people complain too much. What I think we forget is how lucky we are compared to previous generations.","say":"People today complain far too much about their lives. Do you agree?"}],[{"t":"listen","say":"The results are bound to be delayed. The lab has been short-staffed for months, and the new equipment still hasn't arrived. I'd be very surprised if we got anything before the end of the month.","q":"¿Qué espera el hablante?","o":["Que los resultados se retrasen","Que lleguen mañana","Que cancelen el estudio","Que el laboratorio cierre"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"She can't have forgotten the meeting; I reminded her twice this morning. She must have got stuck in traffic, or perhaps her train was cancelled. Either way, she'd have called if it were something serious.","q":"¿Qué cree el hablante sobre la ausencia?","o":["Que debe estar atrapada en el tráfico o su tren se canceló","Que olvidó la reunión","Que está enferma","Que renunció"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"There's a slim chance the match will go ahead, but in all likelihood it'll be postponed. The pitch is completely waterlogged, and more rain is forecast for this afternoon.","q":"¿Qué es lo más probable?","o":["Que aplacen el partido","Que el partido se juegue normal","Que cambien de estadio","Que deje de llover"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"He might well be right, but I'm not entirely convinced. The data he's using is three years old, and the market has changed considerably since then. I'd want to see more recent figures before making a decision.","q":"¿Por qué duda el hablante?","o":["Los datos tienen tres años","Él nunca tiene razón","No hay datos","El mercado no ha cambiado"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"He ___ have left already; his coat is still here.","o":["can't","must","should","mustn't"],"a":0,"x":"Can't have + participio: deducción negativa sobre el pasado."},{"t":"mc","q":"The project is ___ to be finished on time. Everything is going well.","o":["likely","probably","possibly","unlikely"],"a":0,"x":"Be likely to: ser probable."},{"t":"fill","q":"You ___ have told me! I would have helped you. (deber, reproche)","ans":["should","could"],"x":"Should/could have + participio: reproche."},{"t":"oral","text":"There's every likelihood that prices will continue to rise next year."},{"t":"oral","text":"She must have been exhausted after such a long journey."},{"t":"talk","q":"Look at the situation: your friend didn't come to your party and isn't answering the phone. Speculate about what might have happened.","min":27,"keys":[["must have","might have","may have","could have","can't have"]],"model":"She might have fallen asleep, or she may have had a problem at work. She can't have forgotten, because I reminded her yesterday. She must have had a good reason."},{"t":"talk","q":"How likely is it that you will live abroad one day? Use expressions of probability.","min":26,"keys":[["likely","chance","bound to","probably","doubt"]],"model":"I think there's a good chance I'll live abroad one day. It's very likely that my company will send me to Mexico, although I doubt I'll stay there forever."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen and give a nuanced answer: is the speaker right?","min":24,"keys":[["to some extent","partly","it depends","not entirely"]],"model":"To some extent, it's true, because many jobs will change. However, it's not entirely accurate to say most jobs will disappear; new ones will probably appear too.","say":"Artificial intelligence will definitely replace most jobs in the next ten years."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"The study, which followed over two thousand participants for a decade, found a significant correlation between regular exercise and improved memory in later life. However, the authors are careful to note that correlation does not imply causation.","q":"¿Qué advierten los autores?","o":["Que correlación no implica causalidad","Que el ejercicio daña la memoria","Que el estudio fue muy corto","Que no hubo participantes suficientes"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"In this lecture, I'll first outline the main causes of the Industrial Revolution, then examine its social consequences, and finally consider whether we are currently experiencing a comparable transformation.","q":"¿Qué hará al final de la clase?","o":["Considerar si vivimos una transformación comparable","Describir las causas","Examinar las consecuencias sociales","Hacer un examen"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"While previous research has focused largely on urban populations, relatively little attention has been paid to rural communities. This paper aims to address that gap by analysing data from forty villages in the Andean region.","q":"¿Qué vacío intenta llenar el artículo?","o":["La falta de investigación sobre comunidades rurales","La falta de datos urbanos","La historia de los Andes","La economía de las ciudades"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"It could be argued that the policy has been successful, given the fall in unemployment. Nevertheless, a closer look at the figures suggests that much of the new employment is temporary and poorly paid.","q":"¿Qué revela un análisis más detallado?","o":["Que muchos empleos nuevos son temporales y mal pagados","Que el desempleo subió","Que la política fracasó totalmente","Que los salarios mejoraron mucho"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"The results ___ that the treatment is effective.","o":["suggest","are suggesting to","suggests to","suggestion"],"a":0,"x":"Results (plural) suggest that..."},{"t":"mc","q":"___ the limited sample, the findings should be interpreted with caution.","o":["Given","Despite of","Although","Whereas"],"a":0,"x":"Given = dado/considerando."},{"t":"fill","q":"This essay will ___ the advantages and disadvantages of remote work. (examinar)","ans":["examine","discuss","analyse","analyze"],"x":"Verbos típicos de introducción académica."},{"t":"oral","text":"The data suggest a strong correlation between sleep quality and academic performance."},{"t":"oral","text":"It could be argued that the benefits clearly outweigh the drawbacks."},{"t":"talk","q":"Give a short academic-style presentation: what are the causes and effects of traffic in big cities?","min":33,"keys":[["firstly","first of all","to begin with"],["as a result","consequently","therefore"],["in conclusion","to sum up","overall"]],"model":"To begin with, traffic is caused by the growing number of cars and poor public transport. As a result, people waste hours every day and pollution increases. In conclusion, cities need to invest in better transport systems."},{"t":"talk","q":"Summarise a book, article or documentary you found interesting. Mention its main argument and your evaluation.","min":29,"keys":[["argues","claims","suggests","shows"],["however","although","nevertheless"]],"model":"The documentary argues that plastic is one of the biggest threats to the oceans. It shows how small pieces enter the food chain. However, I think it could have offered more practical solutions."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the claim and evaluate it academically.","min":27,"keys":[["evidence","data","research","studies"]],"model":"That claim is too general. The evidence shows that students can learn well online, but research also suggests that they need more self-discipline and that interaction is often weaker.","say":"Online education is just as effective as face-to-face teaching for all students."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"The new manager hit the ground running. Within a week she had streamlined the approval process, which had been a bone of contention for years, and she'd won over even the most sceptical members of the team.","q":"¿Qué logró la nueva gerente?","o":["Simplificó el proceso y convenció al equipo","Despidió a medio equipo","Creó más conflictos","Renunció a la semana"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"I was a bit taken aback by his reaction. I'd only made a light-hearted comment, but he took it to heart and didn't speak to me for the rest of the evening. In hindsight, I should have read the room better.","q":"¿Qué piensa ahora el hablante?","o":["Que debió interpretar mejor el ambiente","Que él exageró sin razón","Que su comentario fue grave","Que no pasó nada"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The report paints a bleak picture of the industry. Profits have plummeted, investment has dried up, and thousands of jobs are on the line. Unless drastic measures are taken, the sector may never recover.","q":"¿Cómo describe el informe la industria?","o":["De forma muy pesimista","Con optimismo","En crecimiento","Estable"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Their proposal is ambitious, to say the least, but I think it's worth exploring. If we can iron out a few issues regarding the budget, it could be a game changer for the whole company.","q":"¿Qué hace falta para que la propuesta funcione?","o":["Resolver algunos problemas del presupuesto","Cambiar todo el equipo","Rechazarla","Esperar un año"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"The negotiations reached a ___ and both sides left the table.","o":["deadlock","breakthrough","milestone","landmark"],"a":0,"x":"Deadlock = punto muerto."},{"t":"mc","q":"We need to ___ the risks before we make a decision.","o":["weigh up","make up","give up","look up"],"a":0,"x":"Weigh up = sopesar."},{"t":"fill","q":"Their success ___ from years of hard work. (derivarse)","ans":["stems","stemmed"],"x":"Stem from = derivarse de."},{"t":"oral","text":"The proposal was met with a great deal of scepticism at first."},{"t":"oral","text":"In hindsight, we should have tackled the problem much earlier."},{"t":"talk","q":"Describe a problem in your workplace or community and how it could be tackled. Use advanced vocabulary.","min":29,"keys":[["tackle","address","deal with"],["mitigate","boost","foster","curb","streamline"]],"model":"One problem in my community is the lack of green spaces. To tackle it, the city could turn empty lots into parks. This would foster a sense of community and help mitigate pollution."},{"t":"talk","q":"Tell a story about a misunderstanding. Use at least two idioms.","min":31,"keys":[["read the room","took it to heart","the last straw","on the same page","in hindsight","taken aback"]],"model":"Once I made a joke about my boss's car and he took it to heart. I was really taken aback. In hindsight, I should have read the room, because he had just had an accident."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the idiom and explain what it means with an example.","min":27,"keys":[["means","for example"]],"model":"It means to start working very quickly and effectively. For example, when I started my new job I hit the ground running and finished my first project in a week.","say":"What does 'to hit the ground running' mean? Give an example."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"I appreciate your offer, but I'm afraid it's not quite what we had in mind. If you could bring the price down by around ten percent, we'd be in a position to commit to a two-year contract.","q":"¿Qué ofrece el comprador a cambio de un descuento?","o":["Un contrato de dos años","Pago en efectivo","Comprar el doble","Recomendarlo a otros"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Let me put it this way: every day we delay this decision, we lose customers to our competitors. I'm not saying the new system is perfect, but it's far better than doing nothing.","q":"¿Qué argumento usa el hablante?","o":["Que retrasar la decisión hace perder clientes","Que el sistema es perfecto","Que no hay competidores","Que es mejor esperar"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"We're willing to be flexible on the delivery dates, but quality is non-negotiable. If you can guarantee that every unit passes our inspection, we can discuss the payment terms.","q":"¿En qué NO negociará?","o":["La calidad","Las fechas de entrega","Las condiciones de pago","El número de unidades"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Imagine waking up every morning without that knot in your stomach. Imagine having time for your family again. That's what our programme offers: not just a new job, but a new life.","q":"¿Qué técnica usa el hablante?","o":["Hacer imaginar al oyente un futuro mejor","Dar estadísticas","Criticar a la competencia","Contar un chiste"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"We'd be prepared to lower the price ___ you order at least 500 units.","o":["provided that","unless","despite","even though"],"a":0,"x":"Provided that = siempre que."},{"t":"mc","q":"I'm afraid that's ___ our budget.","o":["beyond","above to","outside of from","over than"],"a":0,"x":"Beyond our budget = fuera de nuestro presupuesto."},{"t":"fill","q":"Could you ___ any flexibility on the price? (ofrecer)","ans":["offer"],"x":"Offer flexibility = ofrecer flexibilidad."},{"t":"oral","text":"I see where you're coming from, but I'm afraid we can't accept those terms."},{"t":"oral","text":"If you could meet us halfway on the price, we'd be happy to sign today."},{"t":"talk","q":"Negotiate: you want a higher salary in your current job. Make your case to your manager.","min":37,"keys":[["i'd like","i would like"],["because","since"],["if","would"]],"model":"I'd like to talk about my salary. Since I joined, I've taken on more responsibilities and my team has increased sales by twenty percent. If you could raise my salary by ten percent, I would be happy to lead the new project."},{"t":"talk","q":"Persuade a friend to start learning English with you. Use at least three persuasive techniques.","min":32,"keys":[["imagine","think about"],["not only","also"],["you'll","you will"]],"model":"Imagine travelling anywhere and understanding everyone. Not only will English help you get a better job, but it will also make travelling much easier. You'll see results in a few months, and we can practise together."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the offer and respond with a counter-offer.","min":25,"keys":[["appreciate","thank"],["if","could"]],"model":"I appreciate the offer, but it's a bit high for us. If you could lower it to four thousand and include installation, we could sign the contract today.","say":"Our best price is five thousand dollars, without installation. What do you think?"}],[{"t":"listen","say":"The gap between rich and poor has widened considerably over the last three decades. According to the report, the wealthiest one percent now own more than the bottom fifty percent combined, a trend the authors describe as unsustainable.","q":"¿Cómo describen los autores la tendencia?","o":["Insostenible","Positiva","Temporal","Insignificante"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Many older people in rural areas are being left behind by digital services. When banks close local branches and move everything online, those without internet access or digital skills struggle to carry out even basic tasks.","q":"¿Quién sufre con los servicios digitales?","o":["Personas mayores en zonas rurales","Los jóvenes de ciudad","Los empleados bancarios","Las empresas tecnológicas"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Supporters say the sugar tax has reduced consumption of fizzy drinks by almost a third. Critics argue it hits poorer families hardest, since they spend a larger proportion of their income on food.","q":"¿Qué critican del impuesto al azúcar?","o":["Afecta más a las familias pobres","No redujo el consumo","Es demasiado bajo","Solo aplica a restaurantes"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"It's not that young people don't care about politics. Surveys show they're deeply concerned about climate change and inequality. What they don't trust is traditional parties, which they feel don't represent them.","q":"¿En qué no confían los jóvenes?","o":["En los partidos tradicionales","En el cambio climático","En las encuestas","En la política en general"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"The government has been criticised for failing to ___ the housing crisis.","o":["address","assist","attend","arrange"],"a":0,"x":"Address a problem = abordar un problema."},{"t":"mc","q":"Inequality has ___ over the last decade.","o":["widened","enlarged","lengthened","grown up"],"a":0,"x":"The gap widens = la brecha se amplía."},{"t":"fill","q":"Many people are ___ behind by rapid technological change. (dejar)","ans":["left"],"x":"Be left behind = quedarse atrás."},{"t":"oral","text":"Access to quality education remains one of the most effective ways to reduce inequality."},{"t":"oral","text":"The policy has been widely criticised for its impact on low-income families."},{"t":"talk","q":"What is the most serious social problem in your country? Explain its causes and propose a solution.","min":29,"keys":[["because","due to","caused by"],["should","could"],["in my view","in my opinion","i believe"]],"model":"In my view, the most serious problem is inequality. It is caused by unequal access to education and jobs. The government should invest in public schools and support small businesses in rural areas."},{"t":"talk","q":"Should the minimum voting age be lowered to 16? Argue for or against.","min":27,"keys":[["argue","believe","think"],["however","on the other hand","although"]],"model":"I believe the voting age should be lowered to sixteen, because young people are affected by political decisions. However, some argue they are not mature enough, although many adults aren't either."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the statement and respond, considering both sides.","min":27,"keys":[["on the one hand","while","although"],["on the other hand","however"]],"model":"On the one hand, technology has made information available to everyone. On the other hand, it has also increased isolation and the spread of misinformation, so the effect is mixed.","say":"Technology has made society more equal."}]],[[{"t":"listen","say":"Were the board to approve the merger, which seems increasingly unlikely, the two companies would become the largest employer in the region. Should it be rejected, however, both would almost certainly have to make substantial redundancies.","q":"¿Qué pasará probablemente si se rechaza la fusión?","o":["Ambas empresas tendrían que despedir a mucha gente","Serían el mayor empleador de la región","La junta renunciaría","Se fusionarían de todos modos"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Hardly had the minister finished her speech when protesters began shouting from the gallery. Only after security had intervened was the debate allowed to continue, by which point most of the journalists had already left.","q":"¿Cuándo pudo continuar el debate?","o":["Después de que intervino seguridad","Inmediatamente","Al día siguiente","Cuando volvieron los periodistas"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"It's high time the council addressed the parking problem. Were it up to me, I'd ban cars from the centre altogether, but I suspect most residents would rather the council simply built another car park.","q":"¿Qué prefieren, según el hablante, la mayoría de residentes?","o":["Que construyan otro parqueadero","Que prohíban los carros en el centro","Que no hagan nada","Que suban los impuestos"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Much as I admire his ambition, I can't help feeling that he's taken on more than he can handle. Be that as it may, he's the only one with the expertise, so we'll have to trust him for the time being.","q":"¿Por qué confiarán en él?","o":["Porque es el único con la experiencia necesaria","Porque no es ambicioso","Porque ya terminó el trabajo","Porque el hablante lo admira totalmente"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"___ you require any further information, please do not hesitate to contact us.","o":["Should","Would","Had","Were"],"a":0,"x":"Should + sujeto = if (condicional formal invertido)."},{"t":"mc","q":"I'd rather you ___ mention this to anyone.","o":["didn't","don't","won't","not"],"a":0,"x":"Would rather + sujeto + pasado."},{"t":"fill","q":"___ it not been for your help, I would have failed. (inversión)","ans":["had"],"x":"Had it not been for = si no hubiera sido por."},{"t":"oral","text":"Had it not been for her timely intervention, the negotiations would have collapsed."},{"t":"oral","text":"Not until the final results were published did we realise the scale of the problem."},{"t":"talk","q":"Talk about a turning point in history. Use inverted conditionals (Had..., Were..., Should...).","min":30,"keys":[["had","were","should"],["would have","would"]],"model":"Had the internet not been invented, our lives would be completely different. Were we still relying on letters, communication would take weeks. Should technology fail tomorrow, I doubt we would know how to cope."},{"t":"talk","q":"Describe your ideal working conditions using 'I'd rather', 'It's high time' and 'I wish'.","min":29,"keys":[["i'd rather","i would rather"],["it's high time","it is high time"],["i wish"]],"model":"I'd rather work from home three days a week. It's high time companies trusted their employees more. I wish my commute were shorter, and I'd rather my boss didn't send emails at midnight."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the question and answer it with precise, complex grammar.","min":27,"keys":[["had","were","not only","only when","never"]],"model":"Had I been born in a different country, I would probably have a completely different career. Not only would I speak another language, but my values might also be different.","say":"How different would your life be if you had been born in another country?"}],[{"t":"listen","say":"The distinction between 'disinterested' and 'uninterested' is often blurred. A disinterested judge is impartial, having nothing to gain from the outcome; an uninterested judge simply doesn't care, which is, needless to say, far more worrying.","q":"¿Qué significa 'disinterested' según el hablante?","o":["Imparcial, sin nada que ganar","Aburrido, sin interés","Desinformado","Desconfiado"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The minister's statement was deliberately ambiguous. She neither confirmed nor denied the rumours, and her use of phrases such as 'in due course' and 'all options remain on the table' was clearly intended to buy time.","q":"¿Cuál era la intención de la ministra?","o":["Ganar tiempo","Confirmar los rumores","Renunciar","Anunciar una decisión"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Calling the plan 'ambitious' is a polite way of saying it's unrealistic. Calling it 'bold' suggests admiration. Calling it 'reckless' suggests danger. The facts are identical; the connotations are not.","q":"¿Cuál es la idea principal?","o":["Las palabras elegidas cambian la connotación","El plan es peligroso","El plan es realista","Los hechos son diferentes"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Her apology was carefully worded: she regretted 'any offence that may have been caused', which, as critics were quick to point out, is not quite the same as admitting she had done anything wrong.","q":"¿Qué señalaron los críticos?","o":["Que no admitió haber hecho algo mal","Que la disculpa fue sincera","Que no se disculpó","Que renunció"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"The evidence is ___; it could support either interpretation.","o":["ambiguous","ambivalent","obvious","explicit"],"a":0,"x":"Ambiguous = que admite varias interpretaciones."},{"t":"mc","q":"His ___ remarks offended everyone at the table.","o":["tactless","tactful","discreet","diplomatic"],"a":0,"x":"Tactless = sin tacto."},{"t":"fill","q":"She was ___ (imparcial) — she had nothing to gain from the decision.","ans":["disinterested","impartial","unbiased"],"x":"Disinterested = imparcial."},{"t":"oral","text":"The distinction may seem subtle, but it has significant implications."},{"t":"oral","text":"Her remarks were open to interpretation, which was presumably intentional."},{"t":"talk","q":"Explain the difference between two words that people often confuse (for example: economic/economical, sensible/sensitive, actually/currently).","min":25,"keys":[["whereas","while","but"],["means","refers to"]],"model":"Economic refers to the economy, for example economic growth, whereas economical means not wasting money, like an economical car. People often confuse them because they look very similar."},{"t":"talk","q":"Describe the same event twice: first positively, then negatively, choosing words with different connotations.","min":26,"keys":[["but","however","on the other hand"]],"model":"Positively: the new manager is confident, determined and ambitious. Negatively: the new manager is arrogant, stubborn and reckless. The facts are the same, but the words change the impression."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the statement and rephrase it more diplomatically.","min":18,"keys":[["perhaps","might","may","slightly","somewhat"]],"model":"Perhaps the report could be slightly more detailed in some sections, and it might benefit from a few more examples.","say":"Your report is terrible and full of mistakes."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"We shall not be deterred. We shall not be divided. And we shall not rest until every child in this country has access to the education they deserve.","q":"¿Qué recurso retórico usa el discurso?","o":["Repetición (anáfora)","Ironía","Pregunta retórica","Eufemismo"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Oh, brilliant. The train's cancelled again. That's exactly what I needed on the morning of my most important meeting of the year. What a wonderful start to the day.","q":"¿Qué tono usa el hablante?","o":["Sarcasmo","Alegría sincera","Tristeza","Indiferencia"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Ask yourselves: if not us, who? If not now, when? We cannot keep waiting for someone else to solve problems that we ourselves have created.","q":"¿Qué recurso retórico predomina?","o":["Preguntas retóricas","Estadísticas","Anécdota personal","Comparación numérica"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The company didn't exactly cover itself in glory last year. Profits were, shall we say, somewhat disappointing, and the launch of the new product could charitably be described as a learning experience.","q":"¿Qué figura usa el hablante?","o":["Atenuación irónica (understatement)","Hipérbole","Repetición","Metáfora literal"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"'It's raining cats and dogs' is an example of ___.","o":["an idiom","an oxymoron","alliteration","an understatement"],"a":0,"x":"Es un modismo: llueve a cántaros."},{"t":"mc","q":"'Deafening silence' is an example of ___.","o":["an oxymoron","a simile","a pun","an anaphora"],"a":0,"x":"Oxímoron: dos ideas opuestas juntas."},{"t":"fill","q":"Saying 'It's a bit chilly' at minus twenty degrees is an ___. (atenuación)","ans":["understatement"],"x":"Understatement = atenuación irónica."},{"t":"oral","text":"Ask not what your country can do for you; ask what you can do for your country."},{"t":"oral","text":"We shall fight on the beaches, we shall fight on the landing grounds, we shall never surrender."},{"t":"talk","q":"Give a short motivational speech to a team before an important project. Use repetition and at least one rhetorical question.","min":31,"keys":[["we will","we shall","we can"],["?","who","why","what if","if not"]],"model":"Team, if not us, who? We have the talent, we have the experience, and we have the energy. We will prepare, we will deliver, and we will make this the best project of our careers."},{"t":"talk","q":"Describe a frustrating situation using irony or understatement.","min":27,"keys":[["exactly","wonderful","brilliant","a bit","slightly","somewhat"]],"model":"My flight was delayed eight hours, my suitcase went to Paris and my hotel had no reservation. It was, shall we say, a slightly imperfect start to the holiday. Absolutely wonderful."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the quote and explain what rhetorical device it uses and why it is effective.","min":24,"keys":[["contrast","repetition","antithesis","parallel"]],"model":"It uses antithesis, a contrast between two opposite ideas in a parallel structure. It's effective because it's memorable and makes the listener think about their own responsibility.","say":"It was the best of times, it was the worst of times."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"When editing your own work, read it aloud. Your ear will catch clumsy rhythms, repeated words and overlong sentences that your eye skips over. Then cut every word that does not earn its place.","q":"¿Qué recomienda para editar?","o":["Leer en voz alta y cortar palabras innecesarias","Escribir frases más largas","No releer el texto","Usar más adjetivos"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"A strong opening paragraph does three things: it captures the reader's attention, establishes the context and signals where the argument is going. Everything else can wait.","q":"¿Qué NO necesita hacer el primer párrafo?","o":["Presentar todos los detalles","Captar la atención","Establecer el contexto","Indicar hacia dónde va el argumento"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Many writers confuse complexity with sophistication. In reality, the most sophisticated prose is often the simplest, because it reflects a clear understanding of the subject. Obscurity is usually a sign of muddled thinking.","q":"Según el hablante, ¿qué suele indicar la oscuridad en la escritura?","o":["Pensamiento confuso","Inteligencia","Sofisticación","Experiencia"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"In a formal complaint, state the facts first, then the impact on you, and finally what you expect the organisation to do. Remain courteous but firm, and set a reasonable deadline for a response.","q":"¿Cuál es el orden recomendado?","o":["Hechos, impacto, lo que esperas","Lo que esperas, hechos, impacto","Impacto, amenazas, hechos","Saludo, historia personal, despedida"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"Which sentence is the most concise?","o":["We must decide now.","It is necessary for us to make a decision at this point in time.","At this moment in time we need to come to a decision.","A decision is something that needs to be made by us now."],"a":0,"x":"La concisión elimina palabras innecesarias."},{"t":"mc","q":"Which is the most appropriate formal closing when you don't know the recipient's name?","o":["Yours faithfully","Cheers","Love","See you"],"a":0,"x":"Yours faithfully cuando empiezas con Dear Sir or Madam."},{"t":"fill","q":"I am writing ___ regard to your advertisement. (con)","ans":["with","in"],"x":"With regard to / In regard to = con respecto a."},{"t":"oral","text":"I am writing to express my concern regarding the recent changes to the service."},{"t":"oral","text":"I would be grateful if you could respond at your earliest convenience."},{"t":"talk","q":"Dictate the opening paragraph of a formal complaint about a product that broke after one week.","min":33,"keys":[["i am writing","i'm writing"],["regarding","with regard to","concerning"],["would be grateful","would appreciate","expect"]],"model":"I am writing to complain regarding a washing machine I purchased on the third of May, which stopped working after only one week. I would be grateful if you could arrange a replacement or a full refund."},{"t":"talk","q":"Explain, as if to a student, three tips for writing a good essay.","min":27,"keys":[["firstly","first","to begin with"],["secondly","also","moreover"],["finally","lastly"]],"model":"Firstly, plan your ideas before you write. Secondly, make sure each paragraph has one clear main idea. Finally, read your essay aloud and cut any words that are not necessary."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the long sentence and say it again more concisely.","min":6,"keys":[["we","must","need"]],"model":"We need to reduce costs immediately.","say":"Due to the fact that at this present moment in time our costs are increasing, it is absolutely essential that we take action in order to reduce them as soon as possible."}],[{"t":"listen","say":"I take your point, and I don't want to dismiss your concerns. That said, I wonder whether we might be overestimating the risks slightly. Could we perhaps run a small pilot before committing to a full decision?","q":"¿Qué propone el hablante?","o":["Hacer una prueba piloto pequeña","Cancelar el proyecto","Ignorar las preocupaciones","Decidir inmediatamente"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"With respect, I think that's a slight oversimplification. The figures you mention are accurate, but they don't take into account the seasonal variation, which accounts for nearly a third of the change.","q":"¿Qué critica el hablante?","o":["Que no se tuvo en cuenta la variación estacional","Que las cifras son falsas","Que el informe es muy largo","Que no hubo cambios"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"I'm going to stop you there, if I may, because we're running short of time. Could you send the rest of your points by email? I'd hate for them to get lost in the last five minutes of the meeting.","q":"¿Por qué interrumpe el hablante?","o":["Porque se acaba el tiempo","Porque no está de acuerdo","Porque está enojado","Porque no entendió"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Before we draw any conclusions, let's make sure we're all talking about the same thing. When you say 'success', do you mean revenue, customer satisfaction or market share? Because the answer changes depending on which.","q":"¿Qué intenta hacer el hablante?","o":["Aclarar qué significa 'éxito' antes de concluir","Cerrar la reunión","Criticar los resultados","Cambiar de tema"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"Which is the most diplomatic way to disagree?","o":["I see your point, but I wonder if...","You're wrong.","That's nonsense.","No way."],"a":0,"x":"Suavizar el desacuerdo es clave en registro alto."},{"t":"mc","q":"'Could I just come in here?' is used to ___.","o":["interrupt politely","end a meeting","agree strongly","ask for the bill"],"a":0,"x":"Come in = intervenir en una conversación."},{"t":"fill","q":"If I could just play devil's ___ for a moment... (abogado)","ans":["advocate"],"x":"Play devil's advocate = hacer de abogado del diablo."},{"t":"oral","text":"With all due respect, I think we might be overlooking a crucial factor."},{"t":"oral","text":"I take your point, but I'm not entirely convinced that's the best way forward."},{"t":"talk","q":"Disagree diplomatically with this idea: 'Meetings are a waste of time and should be abolished'.","min":32,"keys":[["i see","i take your point","i understand"],["but","however","that said"],["perhaps","might","wonder"]],"model":"I take your point that many meetings are inefficient. That said, I wonder whether abolishing them completely might create other problems. Perhaps we could make them shorter and only invite the people who are really needed."},{"t":"talk","q":"Give constructive feedback to a colleague whose presentation was too long and unclear.","min":27,"keys":[["really","liked","great","good"],["perhaps","might","could"],["suggest","recommend","consider"]],"model":"I really liked your examples, they were very clear. Perhaps you could consider cutting a few slides, because it was a bit long. I'd also suggest starting with your main conclusion."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen and respond as a mediator between two colleagues who disagree.","min":27,"keys":[["both","understand"],["what if","how about","could we","perhaps"]],"model":"I understand both points of view. Ana is worried about the budget and Carlos about the deadline. What if we delivered the most important features first and the rest next month?","say":"Ana says the project is too expensive. Carlos says it will be late if they cut the budget. How would you help them agree?"}],[{"t":"listen","say":"The patient presented with acute chest pain radiating to the left arm. An ECG was performed immediately, and given the findings, the decision was made to transfer him to the cardiology unit for further assessment.","q":"¿Qué decidieron hacer con el paciente?","o":["Trasladarlo a cardiología","Darle de alta","Operarlo inmediatamente","Enviarlo a casa con medicamentos"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"The tenant shall be responsible for all minor repairs, whereas the landlord shall remain liable for structural defects. Either party may terminate this agreement by giving not less than two months' written notice.","q":"¿Quién responde por los defectos estructurales?","o":["El arrendador","El inquilino","Ambos por igual","Nadie"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Our quarterly revenue exceeded forecasts by eight percent, driven mainly by strong performance in the Asian markets. However, rising logistics costs squeezed our margins, so net profit remained broadly flat.","q":"¿Por qué la ganancia neta no subió?","o":["Por el aumento de los costos logísticos","Porque bajaron los ingresos","Por malos resultados en Asia","Por impuestos nuevos"],"a":0},{"t":"listen","say":"Before deploying the update to production, we'll run the full test suite in the staging environment. If any critical bugs are found, we'll roll back and push the release to next sprint.","q":"¿Qué pasa si encuentran errores críticos?","o":["Revertirán y moverán el lanzamiento al siguiente sprint","Lo lanzarán igual","Despedirán al equipo","Cancelarán el producto"],"a":0},{"t":"mc","q":"In a contract, 'shall' usually expresses ___.","o":["an obligation","a suggestion","the future only","a possibility"],"a":0,"x":"En inglés jurídico, shall = obligación."},{"t":"mc","q":"'Revenue' means ___.","o":["ingresos","ganancia neta","deuda","inversión"],"a":0,"x":"Revenue = ingresos totales; profit = ganancia."},{"t":"fill","q":"The doctor ___ (recetar) antibiotics for the infection.","ans":["prescribed"],"x":"Prescribe = recetar."},{"t":"oral","text":"The tenant shall give not less than two months' written notice before terminating the agreement."},{"t":"oral","text":"Revenue exceeded forecasts, although rising costs put pressure on our margins."},{"t":"talk","q":"Explain your job (or a job you know well) using its specialised vocabulary, as if to a new colleague.","min":29,"keys":[["responsible for","in charge of"],["we","our"]],"model":"I work in a call centre as a team leader. I'm responsible for monitoring the agents' performance, checking the average handling time and making sure we meet our service level targets every month."},{"t":"talk","q":"You are a doctor. Explain to a patient, clearly and calmly, a treatment and its risks.","min":33,"keys":[["risk","side effect","chance"],["recommend","suggest","advise"]],"model":"I recommend that you take this medication twice a day for two weeks. The most common side effect is a mild headache, and there is a small chance of nausea. If anything else happens, please call us."},{"t":"talk","q":"Listen to the business update and summarise it in your own words for your boss.","min":20,"keys":[["revenue","sales","profit"],["because","due to","however"]],"model":"Sales went up by ten percent, mainly because of the new online store. However, profit stayed the same due to higher delivery costs.","say":"Quick update: sales rose ten percent this quarter, mostly thanks to the new online store, but profit was flat because delivery costs went up."}]]];
